    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d766">

                <pb facs="0702" n="618" xml:id="pg618"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 872.48/177</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Special Agent in
                        Corfu</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dodge</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-16T15:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 16, 1918, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>From Treasury Department:</p>
                <p>Advised by American Red Cross that Serbian Relief purchases have not been
                    curtailed because of insufficient tonnage and all requirements made by Serbian
                    Minister for foodstuff were promptly taken care of. In very near future further
                    lot of supplies to be shipped weight of which approximates 2,100 tons, and it is
                    expected that ample provision will be made for this space.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
